1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,901
Situated along such a busy trading route it's no surprise that hoi an built an industry around silks suits and ssss dresses.
会安地处繁忙贸易路线，形成了丝绸、西装和连衣裙产业，并不意外。

2
00:00:07,901 --> 00:00:18,212
A staggering 400 tailors fit into this tiny town each offering a personalised outfit unique to your design choices and style.
作者说，小镇里竟有四百家裁缝店，每家都可按你的设计和风格定制服装。

3
00:00:18,212 --> 00:00:25,382
And that's why we found ourselves on chong hung dao the street for a one of a kind outfit.
所以他们来到作者所说的那条街，寻找独一无二的衣服；街名待原声复核。

4
00:00:25,382 --> 00:00:32,270
The process was pretty simple first choose styles you like from literally thousands of photos.
流程很简单，先从数以千计的照片里选喜欢的样式。

5
00:00:32,270 --> 00:00:37,249
Maybe you like the waist of this the length of that the neckline of the other.
也许喜欢这一件的腰身、那一件的长度，和另一件的领口。

6
00:00:37,249 --> 00:00:40,454
Stick all of that together and you have your complete design.
把这些元素组合起来，你的完整设计就有了。

7
00:00:40,454 --> 00:00:46,537
Now as I'm sure you can imagine this was all incredibly exciting for your narrator.
你们想必能想象，对这位旁白来说，这一切有多么令人兴奋。

8
00:00:46,537 --> 00:00:48,566
Second chose your cloth.
第二步，挑选布料；来源字幕时态写作 chose，待原声核验。

9
00:00:48,566 --> 00:00:52,782
This is where we were levelled up and whisked away to the fabrics room.
这时体验升级，我们被迅速领进布料间。

10
00:00:52,782 --> 00:00:55,021
Where there is obviously lots of talk about.
那里显然有很多东西可以讨论；此句原字幕末尾略不完整，待复核。

11
00:00:55,021 --> 00:01:03,920
And it was at this point that I questioned all decisions that had led me to this moment fabrics fabrics fabrics fabrics.
就在这时，我开始反思，究竟哪些决定把我带到了这里：布料、布料，还是布料。

12
00:01:03,920 --> 00:01:15,779
Although brief I did for a second question that maybe just maybe I myself wasn't bringing my full sexy a game ha.
虽然只有一瞬间，我还真的想过，也许我自己的时尚魅力没发挥到最好。

13
00:01:15,779 --> 00:01:19,870
But that was of course just a fleeting moment.
不过那当然只是转瞬即逝的念头。

14
00:01:19,870 --> 00:01:23,532
It was as quick as the next morning where chiaki returned for a final fitting.
很快到了第二天早上，Chiaki 回去做最后一次试衣。

15
00:01:23,532 --> 00:01:26,984
And we picked it up all finished a day later.
再过一天，我们就取到了做好的衣服。

16
00:01:34,194 --> 00:01:38,331
Probably the most iconic landmark in hoi an is the japanese bridge.
会安可能最有代表性的地标，是日本桥。

17
00:01:38,331 --> 00:01:43,989
Indeed if you ever look at the back of a 20 000 dong note you'll see it for yourself.
看看两万越南盾纸币的背面，就能亲眼看到它。

18
00:01:43,989 --> 00:01:49,330
Built in the 15 th century it was constructed by those same japanese merchants who settled here.
作者说这座桥建于十五世纪，由在此定居的日本商人建造。

19
00:01:49,330 --> 00:01:53,601
Seeking quick access to the chinese communities across the water.
他们希望更快地到达水对岸的华人社区。

20
00:01:53,601 --> 00:01:59,201
The bridge represents namazu a giant underground catfish which was said to cause earthquakes.
作者讲到 Namazu 的传说：这是一条地下巨鲶，据说会引发地震。

21
00:01:59,201 --> 00:02:06,739
And was therefore tied down at both ends unable to move namazu could no longer cause the ground beneath it to shake.
于是传说中它两端被固定，不能动，也就无法让地面震动。

22
00:02:24,750 --> 00:02:30,586
After some more aimless meandering we wandered into this cafe and it was time to taste another vietnamese staple.
又漫无目的地逛了一会儿，我们走进这家咖啡店，准备尝尝另一种越南常见饮品。

23
00:02:30,586 --> 00:02:33,758
The egg coffee or c ph trung.
就是蛋咖啡；越南语名称在原字幕中有缺字，待核。

24
00:02:33,758 --> 00:02:40,364
Is a bitter coffee blended with the sweetness of egg yolk condensed milk and sugar.
苦咖啡里加入蛋黄、炼乳和糖的甜味。

25
00:02:40,364 --> 00:02:45,465
This necessity came about with milk being in short supply during french colonisation.
作者说，这种做法与法国殖民时期牛奶短缺有关。

26
00:02:45,465 --> 00:02:51,790
You can still actually visit the place where the original egg coffee was invented in hanoi.
按他的介绍，在河内还能去最初发明蛋咖啡的地方。

27
00:02:51,790 --> 00:02:57,596
Let's just say we filmed this a few times and this was the most positive reaction I had.
这段我们拍了好几次，而这是我最正面的反应了。

28
00:02:57,596 --> 00:03:02,487
It's a really bitter coffee albeit with a dense creamy layer on top.
咖啡确实很苦，不过上面有一层浓厚绵密的奶沫感。

29
00:03:02,487 --> 00:03:07,773
But I'm just a low life single shot latte guy so what do I know.
但我只是个爱喝单份浓缩拿铁的普通人，又懂什么呢。
